Tested on Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.

Installs Postfix (to listen on localhost only) and a pinned Linux GophishFR binary. setcap is used to allow the GophishFR binary to listen on privileged ports without running as root.

1) Edit hosts file with the GophishFR server IP.

2) Edit vars/main.yml with any changes. Set `gophishfr_release_tag` and the
SHA-256 digest of its Linux 64-bit release archive in
`gophishfr_release_sha256`; deployment stops if either pin is missing:

Existing deployments keep the `gophish_deploy` working directory so relative
database and log paths continue to use the current data. The role replaces the
legacy `gophish.service` unit with `gophishfr.service`.

3) Modify files/config.json with any changes.

4) Execute

# Log in as root with SSH key
ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts -u root --private-key=private.key

# Log in as root with password
ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts -u root --ask-pass

# Log in as non-root user with SSH key (if root login has been disabled)
ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts --private-key=private.key -u user --become --ask-become-pass

# Logging in as non-root user without SSH keys
ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts -u ubuntu --ask-pass --become --ask-become-pass
